ayuktaḥ kāmakāreṇa phale sakto nibadhyate', 'He who is possessed of devotion, abandoning the fruit of actions, attains the highest tranquillity. He who is without devotion, and attached to the fruit (of action), is tied down by (reason of his) acting in consequence of (some) desire.');
